{
	"type": "root",
	"children": [
		{
			"type": "yaml",
			"value": "title: Intercepting Routes\ndescription: Use intercepting routes to load a new route within the current layout while masking the browser URL, useful for advanced routing patterns such as modals."
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Intercepting routes allows you to load a route from another part of your application within the current layout. This routing paradigm can be useful when you want to display the content of a route without the user switching to a different context."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "For example, when clicking on a photo in a feed, you can display the photo in a modal, overlaying the feed. In this case, Next.js intercepts the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "/photo/123"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " route, masks the URL, and overlays it over "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "/feed"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "html",
					"value": "<Image\nalt=\"Intercepting routes soft navigation\"\nsrcLight=\"/docs/light/intercepting-routes-soft-navigate.png\"\nsrcDark=\"/docs/dark/intercepting-routes-soft-navigate.png\"\nwidth=\"1600\"\nheight=\"617\"\n/>"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "However, when navigating to the photo by clicking a shareable URL or by refreshing the page, the entire photo page should render instead of the modal. No route interception should occur."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "html",
					"value": "<Image\nalt=\"Intercepting routes hard navigation\"\nsrcLight=\"/docs/light/intercepting-routes-hard-navigate.png\"\nsrcDark=\"/docs/dark/intercepting-routes-hard-navigate.png\"\nwidth=\"1600\"\nheight=\"604\"\n/>"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Convention"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Intercepting routes can be defined with the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "(..)"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " convention, which is similar to relative path convention "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "../"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " but for route segments."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "You can use:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "(.)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " to match segments on the "
								},
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "same level"
										}
									]
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "(..)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " to match segments "
								},
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "one level above"
										}
									]
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "(..)(..)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " to match segments "
								},
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "two levels above"
										}
									]
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "(...)"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " to match segments from the "
								},
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "root"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " "
								},
								{
									"type": "inlineCode",
									"value": "app"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " directory"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "For example, you can intercept the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "photo"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " segment from within the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "feed"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " segment by creating a "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "(..)photo"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " directory."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "html",
					"value": "<Image\nalt=\"Intercepting routes folder structure\"\nsrcLight=\"/docs/light/intercepted-routes-files.png\"\nsrcDark=\"/docs/dark/intercepted-routes-files.png\"\nwidth=\"1600\"\nheight=\"604\"\n/>"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "blockquote",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "paragraph",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "strong",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Good to know:"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " The "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "(..)"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " convention is based on "
						},
						{
							"type": "emphasis",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "route segments"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": ", not the file-system. For example, it does not consider "
						},
						{
							"type": "inlineCode",
							"value": "@slot"
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": " folders in "
						},
						{
							"type": "link",
							"title": null,
							"url": "./parallel-routes.md",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Parallel Routes"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "."
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 2,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Examples"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "heading",
			"depth": 3,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Modals"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Intercepting Routes can be used together with "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
					"url": "./parallel-routes.md",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "Parallel Routes"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " to create modals. This allows you to solve common challenges when building modals, such as:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "list",
			"ordered": false,
			"start": null,
			"spread": false,
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "Making the modal content "
								},
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "shareable through a URL"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Preserving context"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " when the page is refreshed, instead of closing the modal."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Closing the modal on backwards navigation"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": " rather than going to the previous route."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "listItem",
					"spread": false,
					"checked": null,
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"children": [
								{
									"type": "strong",
									"children": [
										{
											"type": "text",
											"value": "Reopening the modal on forwards navigation"
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"value": "."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "Consider the following UI pattern, where a user can open a photo modal from a gallery using client-side navigation, or navigate to the photo page directly from a shareable URL:"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "html",
					"value": "<Image\nalt=\"Intercepting routes modal example\"\nsrcLight=\"/docs/light/intercepted-routes-modal-example.png\"\nsrcDark=\"/docs/dark/intercepted-routes-modal-example.png\"\nwidth=\"1600\"\nheight=\"976\"\n/>"
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "In the above example, the path to the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "photo"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " segment can use the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "(..)"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " matcher since "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "@modal"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " is a slot and "
				},
				{
					"type": "strong",
					"children": [
						{
							"type": "text",
							"value": "not"
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " a segment. This means that the "
				},
				{
					"type": "inlineCode",
					"value": "photo"
				},
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": " route is only one segment level higher, despite being two file-system levels higher."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"type": "paragraph",
			"children": [
				{
					"type": "text",
					"value": "See the "
				},
				{
					"type": "link",
					"title": null,
